\end{align*}Since $m$ is an integer, $\frac{100-4n}{3}$ must be an integer. This occurs when $100-4n$ is divisible by $3$. The smallest value of $n$ that makes $100-4n$ divisible by $3$ is $n=1$. Then $100-4n=100-4=96$ is not divisible by $3$, so $n=1$ is the smallest value that makes $100-4n$ divisible by $3$. Then $m=\frac{100-4(1)}{3}=\frac{96}{3}=32$. Thus, the minimum value of $\left| m - n \right|$ is $\left|32-1\right|=\boxed{31}$.

