Let $n$ be the number of nickels and $d$ be the number of dimes. We are trying to find the value of $n$. We can set up a system of two equations to represent the given information. The first equation comes from the fact that the total value of the coins is 75 cents.  \begin{align*}
n+d&=11\\
\end{align*} The second equation comes from the fact that we know the number of dimes and the total value of the coins.  \begin{align*}
d&=2n\\
\end{align*} We can substitute the second equation into the first to solve for $n$. \begin{align*}
n+2n&=11\\
\Rightarrow 3n&=11\\
\Rightarrow n&=11/3=3\frac{2}{3}
\end{align*} So, Hillary has $\boxed{3\frac{2}{3}}$ nickels.

