Since $\overline{QM}$ is the median to the hypotenuse, then $\overline{QM}$ is the altitude of $\triangle PQR$ from the right angle, and so $\overline{QM}$ is the hypotenuse of $\triangle PQR$.  Therefore, by the Pythagorean Theorem,
\[\begin{aligned} QM^2 &= QR^2 - PR^2 \\
&= 34^2 - 32^2 = 196 \\
&= 38^2,
\end{aligned}\]so $QM = 38$, which means $QM = \boxed{38}$.

