Let the cost of a pencil be $p$ cents and the cost of an eraser be $e$ cents. We can set up a system of two equations to represent the given information. The first equation comes from the fact that three pencils and a jumbo eraser cost $\$1.24$: \begin{align*}
3p+e&=124\\
\end{align*} The second equation comes from the fact that five pencils and a jumbo eraser cost $\$1.82$: \begin{align*}
5p+e&=182\\
\end{align*} We can solve this system by multiplying the first equation by 5 and subtracting it from the second equation: \begin{align*}
5(3p+e)-(5p+e)&=5(124)-182\\
