p&=24
\end{align*} So, a pencil costs $\boxed{24}$ cents.

By Cauchy-Schwarz,
\[(a + b + c + d) \left( \frac{1}{a} + \frac{1}{b} + \frac{4}{c} + \frac{16}{d} \right) \ge (1 + 1 + 4 + 16)^2 = 256.\]Hence,
\[\frac{1}{a} + \frac{1}{b} + \frac{4}{c} + \frac{16}{d} \ge 256/a + 256/b + 256/c + 256/d.\]By AM-GM,
\[256/a + 256/b + 256/c + 256/d \ge 4 \sqrt[4]{256 \cdot 256 \cdot 256 \cdot 256} = 256,\]so
\[\frac{1}{a} + \frac{1}{b} + \frac{4}{c} + \frac{16}{d} \ge 256/a + 256/b + 256/c + 256/d \ge 256.\]Equality occurs when $a = b = c = d = 1/4.$

[asy]
unitsize(0.5 cm);

pair A, B, C, D;

A = (1,1);
B = (1,2);
C = (2,2);
D = (2,1);

draw(A--B--C--D--cycle);
draw(A--(A + B + C + D)/4--(A + B + C + D)/4);
draw(A--(A + B + C)/4--(A + B + C)/4);

label("$a$", (A + B + C)/4, W);
label("$b$", (A + B + C)/4, NW);
label("$c$", (A + B + C)/4, SW);
label("$d$", (A + B + C)/4, SE);
[/asy]

Hence, the minimum value is $\boxed{256}.$

