\cline{2-10}
x-1 & x^9 & & & & & & & \\
\multicolumn{2}{r}{x^8} & -x^7 & & & & & & \\
\cline{2-3}
\multicolumn{2}{r}{x^7} & +x^6 & & & & & & \\
\multicolumn{2}{r}{x^7} & -x^6 & & & & & & \\
\cline{3-4}
\multicolumn{2}{r}{x^6} & +x^5 & & & & & & \\
\multicolumn{2}{r}{x^6} & -x^5 & & & & & & \\
\cline{4-5}
\multicolumn{2}{r}{x^5} & +x^4 & & & & & & \\
\multicolumn{2}{r}{x^5} & -x^4 & & & & & & \\
\cline{5-6}
\multicolumn{2}{r}{x^4} & +x^3 & & & & & & \\
\multicolumn{2}{r}{x^4} & -x^3 & & & & & & \\
\cline{6-7}
\multicolumn{2}{r}{x^3} & +x^2 & & & & & & \\
\multicolumn{2}{r}{x^3} & -x^2 & & & & & & \\
\cline{7-8}
\multicolumn{2}{r}{x^2} & +x & & & & & & \\
\multicolumn{2}{r}{x^2} & -x & & & & & & \\
\cline{8-9}
\multicolumn{2}{r}{x} & +1 & & & & & & \\
\multicolumn{2}{r}{x} & -1 & & & & & & \\
\cline{9-10}
\multicolumn{2}{r}{1} & & & & & & & \\
\end{array}
\]

So, the quotient is $x^8 + x^7 + x^6 + x^5 + x^4 + x^3 + x^2 + x + 1.$

Note: We can use long division to divide $x^9 + 1$ by $x - 1,$ but it is easier to use the fact that $x^9 + 1$ is the sum of the cubes of the odd-indexed powers of $x,$ so
\begin{align*}
x^9 + 1 &= x^9 + 2x^7 + 2x^5 + 2x^3 + 2x + 1 \\
&= (x^9 - 2x^7 + 2x^5 - 2x^3 + 2x) + (2x^7 + 2x^5 + 2x^3 + 2x + 1) \\
&= x^7 + 2x^5 + 2x^3 + 2x + 1.
\end{align*}Then by the same reasoning as above, the quotient is $x^7 + 2x^5 + 2x^3 + 2x + 1.$

