Let $\mathbf{v} = \begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ -1 \end{pmatrix}.$  Then $\mathbf{M} \mathbf{v} = \begin{pmatrix} 9 \\ 3 \end{pmatrix}.$  Also, $\mathbf{M} \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ -3 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 7 \\ -1 \end{pmatrix}.$

[asy]
unitsize(0.5 cm);

pair A, B, C, D, E, F, M, V;

A = (2,1);
B = (0,0);
C = (3,0);
D = (0,2);
E = (1,2);
F = (1,0);
M = (1.5,1);
V = (1,2);

draw(A--B--C--D--E--F--cycle);
draw(M--V);

label("$\mathbf{v}$", V, S);
label("$\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ -1 \end{pmatrix}$", A, W);
label("$\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ -3 \end{pmatrix}$", B, S);
label("$\begin{pmatrix} 9 \\ 3 \end{pmatrix}$", M, N);
label("$\begin{pmatrix} 7 \\ -1 \end{pmatrix}$", C, S);
[/asy]

Then $\mathbf{M} \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ -3 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 7 \\ -1 \end{pmatrix}.$  We can write
\[\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ -3 \end{pmatrix} = \mathbf{v} + \mathbf{w},\]where $\mathbf{v} = \begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ -1 \end{pmatrix}$ and $\mathbf{w} = \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ -5 \end{pmatrix}.$  Then
\[\mathbf{M} \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ -3 \end{pmatrix} = \mathbf{M} \mathbf{v} + \mathbf{M} \mathbf{w}.\]Since $\mathbf{M} \mathbf{v} = \begin{pmatrix} 9 \\ 3 \end{pmatrix},$
\[\mathbf{M} \mathbf{w} = \begin{pmatrix} 9 \\ 3 \end{pmatrix} - \begin{pmatrix} 7 \\ -1 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ 4 \end{pmatrix}.\]Thus,
\[\mathbf{M} \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ -3 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 9 \\ 3 \end{pmatrix} + \begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ 4 \end{pmatrix} = \boxed{\begin{pmatrix} 11 \\ 7 \end{pmatrix}}.\]

